3. Detailed Module Breakdown
The 28 feature modules in src/modules are grouped below by domain area:
A. Identity, Authentication & Security
Module	Location	Responsibilities & Description
AuthModule	src/modules/auth	Manages user registration, login, JWT token generation, refresh tokens, and password reset requests. Uses Argon2 for password hashing and Passport strategies for JWT guards.
UserModule	src/modules/user	Handles user profile CRUD operations, avatar management, user status toggles (active/blocked), and user search capabilities. Includes user.gateway.ts for online status tracking.
RoleModule	src/modules/role	Implements Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). Defines roles (e.g., Student, Instructor, Admin, SuperAdmin) and associated permissions.
GroupModule	src/modules/group	Manages student cohorts/batches. Allows grouping users together for batch course enrollment, targeted assessments, and group progress monitoring.
B. Core Course Architecture & Content Delivery
Module	Location	Responsibilities & Description
CategoryModule	src/modules/category	Manages course taxonomies, parent-child categories, and subject classifications to enable easy course discovery.
CourseModule	src/modules/course	Primary course engine handling creation, title, slugification, descriptions, thumbnail metadata, pricing, publication workflow (draft/published), and assigned instructors.
CoursemoduleModule	src/modules/coursemodule	Organizes courses into high-level structural units/modules (e.g. "Module 1: Introduction to Web Dev").
ChapterModule	src/modules/chapter	Represents individual chapters/lessons nested under a course module. Stores sequence order, estimated completion time, and chapter metadata.
ChaptercontentModule	src/modules/chaptercontent	Stores text-based lesson contents, downloadable PDF attachments, external resource links, and supplementary reading material.
ChapterVideoModule	src/modules/chapter-video	Handles video lesson metadata, stream URLs, AWS S3 storage keys, duration tracking, and video resolution formats.
C. Assessment & Evaluation Engine
Module	Location	Responsibilities & Description
QuestionBankModule	src/modules/question-bank	Central repository of reusable questions categorized by difficulty, subject, and topic for quick assessment creation.
AssessmentModule	src/modules/assessment	Manages test/quiz templates, time limits, total marks, passing thresholds, negative marking rules, and attempt limits.
AssessmentQuestionsModule	src/modules/assessment-questions	Links specific questions (MCQ, True/False, Subjective) to an assessment, handling question ordering and weightages.
AnswerOptionsModule	src/modules/answer-options	Manages individual answer options for multiple-choice questions, specifying correct keys and feedback messages.
CourseAssessmentModule	src/modules/course-assessment	Binds assessments to specific courses, modules, or chapters (e.g. Chapter End Quiz, Course Final Exam).
StudentAssessmentModule	src/modules/student-assessment	Tracks live student test sessions, start/end timestamps, countdown timers, tab-switch alerts, and attempt state machine.
StudentSubmissionModule	src/modules/student-submission	Stores submitted student answers, handles automatic grading for MCQs, and provides instructor evaluation interfaces for subjective answers.
D. Real-Time Interaction & Student Engagement
Module	Location	Responsibilities & Description
CourseDiscussionModule	src/modules/course-discussion	Course-wide QA & discussion forum. Contains course-discussion.gateway.ts for live real-time comment streams via WebSockets.
ChapterVideoCommentsModule	src/modules/chapter-video-comments	In-video discussion threads. Includes chapter-video-comment.gateway.ts allowing real-time chat anchored to specific video playback timestamps.
ChapterVideoNotesModule	src/modules/chapter-video-notes	Personal student notebook feature. Allows students to save timestamped notes while watching video lectures.
NotificationModule	src/modules/notification	Notification dispatch engine. Uses notification.gateway.ts for real-time WebSocket push alerts and database notification persistence.
E. Operations, Analytics & Platform Infrastructure
Module	Location	Responsibilities & Description
AdmindashboardModule	src/modules/admindashboard	Provides aggregated metrics and analytics for admins (active users, total enrollments, revenue, course completion stats).
SubscribeModule	src/modules/subscribe	Manages course subscriptions, enrollment records, student access grants, and expiration dates.
FileUploadModule	src/modules/file-upload	Integrates with AWS S3 for uploading avatars, course thumbnails, video files, and student submission attachments.
EmailModule	src/modules/email	Wrapper around SendGrid and Nodemailer for sending transactional emails (welcome emails, password resets, enrollment notices).
SchedulerModule	src/modules/scheduler	Cron job runner using @nestjs/schedule for background maintenance, automatic assessment timeouts, and cleanup tasks.
LogModule	src/modules/log	Intercepts HTTP requests via LoggerInterceptor to log API request/response metadata, execution time, and error trace logs into MongoDB.
MiscModule	src/modules/misc	Utility endpoints for platform configurations, system health checks, and global metadata lookup.
4. Key Request Lifecycle & Design Conventions
1. Global Routing Prefix: All REST endpoints are prefixed with /api (configured in main.ts).
2. Response Standardization: Controllers leverage responseBuilder and customErrorBuilder located in src/utils/ to ensure predictable JSON response payloads across all endpoints.
3. Authentication Guarding: Protected endpoints use @UseGuards(AuthGuard('jwt')). The authenticated payload is extracted using the custom @User() decorator from src/common/decorators.
4. Validation Pipeline: DTOs use class-validator and class-transformer annotations. The global ValidationPipe validates incoming payloads before controller execution.
5. Real-time Gateways: Socket.IO gateways (.gateway.ts) maintain client connections across user, notification, course-discussion, and chapter-video-comments.


